494:Despite being a splendid, relaxing summer day, the atmosphere inside the Mahjong Soul Shrine is as oppressive as if thunderclouds were looming, and everyone looks nervous... I'd just stepped into the room to bring Ichihime some snacks, but upon seeing the scene before me, I take a deep breath and have a hunch.
2:player
3:{character:player}It must be that girl who's been coming here a lot recently that created such a heavy atmosphere, like "the devil's in the house."
5:{character:Chiori Mikami}Yakuman!
6:Sure enough, I'd barely finished speaking when I spot the blonde girl playing a lively match, her conspicuous red hairband like a warning to strangers to approach at their own peril.
7:Glancing at the table, the number of scattered scoring sticks clearly indicates that Chiori Mikami has just totally crushed her opponents.
8:Chiori Mikami
9:{character:Chiori Mikami}Hmph, all bark but no bite. Talked a big game but really, what a disappointment. Just now, who was just flapping their gums, saying they were gonna take Chiori down a peg or two?
10:Amongst the watching crowd's admiration for Chiori Mikami, the Jyanshi opposite stands up dejectedly from the table, a grudging and awkward smile on their face.
11:Jyanshi A
12:{character:Jyanshi A}Hey, we let you win. Otherwise you'd probably cry or something.
13:Jyanshi B & Jyanshi C
14:{character:Jyanshi B & Jyanshi C}Yeah! That's right!
15:Hearing this excuse, the other two Jyanshi nod frantically. Chiori Mikami's expression suddenly darkens.
17:{character:Chiori Mikami}Huh? Let me win? You three "glass fogeys"?
18:Jyanshi C
19:{character:Jyanshi C}Glass?
20:{character:Chiori Mikami}Your tactics and your tiles are like glass - I can see right through them.
21:Jyanshi B
22:{character:Jyanshi B}Er... Haha, can't you take a joke, kid? Don't need to take it so seriously, eh?
23:{character:Chiori Mikami}Back at you! After all, you looked a lot more serious when finding an excuse than playing!
24:Chiori Mikami unceremoniously calls them out, and the surrounding crowd gradually grows louder, showing that everyone else has issues with what the three Jyanshi had said, too. Their expressions grow more and more embarrassed, first blushing red and then turning pale as they pathetically hang their heads.
25:{character:Jyanshi A}Sorry, we were being petty. I apologize.
26:{character:Chiori Mikami}Instead of apologizing, get out of here and practice. I've lost count of the number of Jyanshi I've met who are all talk and no action.
27:Through a chorus of boos, the three red-faced Jyanshi leave in a hurry. Having watched the whole scene, I can't help but let out a sigh.
28:{character:player}So cocky... It wouldn't be surprising if she gets bundled into a sack one day while walking along the road.
29:While One Han City has always been peaceful, it's precisely because it is One Han City that you shouldn't get on the wrong side of a Jyanshi.
31:{character:Riu Kujou}Do you really think I'd let that happen?
32:{character:player}Riu? When did you get here?
33:The girl who silently appeared at my side is Riu Kujou, Chiori Mikami's maid. They're like sisters, despite one working for the other.
34:As Chiori's personal maid, Riu Kujou excels at forcibly defending her lady's honor, punishing anyone who disrespects or even has inappropriate thoughts about her. I've tasted the power of those iron fists myself on several occasions, when I've dared joke about Chiori Mikami.
35:...Hang on. I suddenly recall my kind of unthinking words just now, and feel some misgivings.
36:
37:{character:player}Riu, what I said just now, about the sack... will you let me explain?
38:Riu Kujou
39:{character:Riu Kujou}What, do, YOU, think?
40:With a tight-lipped smile, Riu Kujou puts her powerful hands firmly on my shoulder.
41:{character:Riu Kujou}However, there's something more important to discuss with you right now.
42:"Boohoo... you just wait, someone's gonna come give you your just deserts..."
44:Seeing yet another Jyanshi run off in tears after being soundly thrashed by Chiori Mikami, I silently look back. Against the backdrop of her arrogant laughter, I look earnestly toward Riu Kujou's serious face.
45:{character:player}You see? Everyone says some inflammatory things in the heat of the moment. But you have to believe me, it was just words, and it's not like I really have a sack at hand!
46:{character:Riu Kujou}Shh-- hush now. What do you think a delicate girl like me could do to you?
47:{character:player}Are you redefining "delicate"...?
48:{character:Riu Kujou}Ah, there was a sudden gust of wind. What did you just say?
49:{character:player}Nothing.
50:{character:Riu Kujou}Uh-huh. Okay then. Let's get down to business, there's a matter that's giving me a bit of a headache that I want to discuss with you.
51:{character:player}Oh? Please, let me know if there's anything I can do to help.
52:Very rarely is the word "headache" ever heard from the mouth of the almost-omnipotent Riu Kujou, so it must be a really tricky problem.
53:{character:Riu Kujou}...A scoundrel. Especially dangerous.
55:{character:Riu Kujou}Why do you look so surprised? Wouldn't the existence of someone so dazzling as Miss Chiori be noticed by such a person?
56:{character:player}What I mean is, don't panic. You can take care of it.
59:{character:player}I see. But your tone tells me that things are a little different this time?
60:{character:Riu Kujou}Well, it was one night about a week ago. I called Miss Chiori to come down for dinner, but then something strange happened...
61:Riu Kujou describes the scene on that day for me.
62:{character:Riu Kujou}Dinner's ready, Miss... Miss Chiori?
63:Surprsingly, Chiori Mikami's bedroom is completely empty.
64:Riu Kujou's just about to go looking elsewhere, when *creak* a noise suddenly comes from the balcony. She looks over to see the sliding glass door open a crack, letting the sultry summer heat seep inside.
65:And the noise sounded like a creak from somebody on a swing.
66:{character:Riu Kujou}What are you doing on the balcony in this heat? Miss Chiori? Umm?
67:Thinking she's found her lady, Riu Kujou goes to the balcony, where she's left shocked and surprised. For there's no sign of Chiori Mikami, only the swing, moving by itself. The air is so dry and still, without even the slightest breeze. She steps forward and touches the seat of the swing, and finds it still warm.
68:Riu Kujou picks up a teddy bear that has fallen beside the swing, her expression serious.
70:{character:Chiori Mikami}Nice, big win! I knew I couldn't lose on my home ground! Riu...
71:Just then, Chiori Mikami's voice comes from outside the bedroom, revealing her actual location to be the small study next door.
72:Riu Kujou clears her head, hurriedly replaces the teddy bear onto the swing, and then runs out of the bedroom in response to Chiori's call.
73:{character:Riu Kujou}I'm here.
74:{character:Chiori Mikami}I just played a South Wind round, and am so hungry I think I could eat even more than Ichihime.
75:{character:Riu Kujou}Pff, I hear you. Tonight I've prepared beef pizza, and sour and spicy prawns, with a mango crepe cake for dessert. If that's not enough, I can also rustle up some pasta.
76:{character:Chiori Mikami}Wow! Are they the sour and spicy prawns we had at the restaurant last time? You learned how to make them, Riu?!
77:{character:Riu Kujou}I hope the taste will be as you remember, Miss.
78:{character:Chiori Mikami}Have some confidence! I'm sure what you make will be even better than the restaurant!
79:{character:Riu Kujou}With those words, Miss Chiori, I'll definitely make something more delicious.
80:{character:Riu Kujou}I'm very flattered that Miss Chiori ate all the shrimp I made that day.
81:{character:player}Whoa, they must have been amazing... Hang on, isn't the point of all this to tell me about this "scoundrel"?
82:{character:Riu Kujou}Oh, yeah! So anyway, that was the first time I learned of their existence. Afterward, there were several times when I was out with Miss Chiori and I felt like someone was spying on us from the shadows. A shame that they seemed pretty alert though, as they'd always disappeared before I could find them.
83:{character:player}Sounds stressful.
85:{character:Riu Kujou}Although I've already enrolled in the latest Special Maid Training class to sharpen my anti-surveillance skills, I don't think I can fully guarantee Miss Chiori's safety this time.
86:{character:player}You're already awesome, Riu. As far as I can tell, Chiori's always been well protected by you. But now that I know what's going on, what can I do to help?
87:{character:Riu Kujou}Join me to increase Miss Chiori's level of protection! If we share the work, we might even catch that scoundrel quicker!
88:{character:player}I'd be happy to, but why choose me, Riu?
89:{character:Riu Kujou}It wasn't so much me who chose you, but rather it was Miss Chiori's "consciousness" that chose you.
90:{character:player}Huh? What's that supposed to mean?
91:{character:Riu Kujou}Miss Chiori is not someone who easily trusts others. Despite seeming to dislike you whenever she sees you, she does always subconsciously seek your help when encountering any problems...
92:{character:Riu Kujou}Perhaps she doesn't even know herself when she formed this habit...
93:{character:Riu Kujou}So I reckon that she might be more likely to let you stay by her side.
94:{character:Riu Kujou}But worry not! It may have been my mistake that made Miss Chiori depend on an outsider, but I'll definitely make things right, and she'll be gone of you in no time!
95:That last sentence sent a shiver up my spine.
96:{character:player}Ahaha... Don't take things so seriously, for real.
97:{character:player}However... it doesn't matter if this scoundrel is a stalker, or has some other purpose. We'd better find them together as soon as possible.
98:{character:Riu Kujou}Shh-- keep your voice down! Miss Chiori herself still doesn't know about all this.
99:{character:player}Huh?
100:{character:Riu Kujou}If she found out, I just know she'd be so scared that she wouldn't eat or sleep. The most important thing is, from my understanding of her, that the lady would even think up a way to catch the scoundrel herself. And that's just too dangerous!
101:{character:Riu Kujou}So, you've gotta think up a reason to come with us.
102:{character:player}Eh... can't I just say I want to spend time with you two?
103:{character: Chiori Mikami}Spend time together? Why would I want to spend time with {var:player_nickname}?
104:{character:Chiori Mikami}Hmph. I don't. So forget it.
105:{character:player}... ...
106:Great. But at least it's not unexpected, and actually pretty normal considering it's Chiori Mikami. Riu Kujou stands by, trying to rescue our protection plan which is in danger of failing before it even starts.
107:{character:Riu Kujou}Didn't you say you wanted to arrange a time to see {var:player_nickname} when you had time, Miss Chiori?
108:{character:Chiori Mikami}Huh?! You're a fool, Riu! I've never, ever said that!
109:{character:Riu Kujou}Ah, I remember now. My mistake. How could you ever want to spend time with {var:player_nickname}, Miss Chiori.
110:I shoot a puzzled look at Riu Kujou, since we're meant to be on the same team and all now.
111:Well, I've gotta do all I can to keep Chiori Mikami safe.
112:{character:player}Why don't you want to hang out with me, Chiori?
113:{character:Chiori Mikami}I just don't feel like it. What's with all the "whys"?!
114:{character:Chiori Mikami}But you really want to see me so badly, {var:player_nickname}? That can't be because... you don't have any friends willing to spend time with you?
115:{character:player}Of course not! I came specially to look for you, Chiori. I even had to turn down other invitations!
116:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Hmph. Don't think you can fool me so easily. If it's not because you don't have other friends, then there has to be some other reason. Come clean!
117:Seems like I have to come up with a good enough reason to make her believe... Alright, let's just say...
144:After waving goodbye to Riu Kujou who kept looking back, I notice Chiori Mikami staring at me. The look in her eyes seems to scream "I see through everything."
164:I obediently cover my ears, and can only see Chiori Mikami say something with her back to me. Not long after, the bushes in front of me shake for a moment and several "fluffy balls" of different colors pop out.
165:As the saying goes, "no risk, no reward." I can't just obey because she's smart. Pretending to keep my ears covered, I wait until Chiori Mikami turns away for a second then quietly move my hands.
166:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Meow-- meow-- meow--
167:The light of the setting sun glints on the hair of the girl beside me, shimmering with a gentle gold. She actually mimics a cat's meow, and her soft voice tickles my heart.
168:{character:Chiori Mikami}It's me! I've brought you some tasty snacks, so come on out, little ones.
169:This is the first time I've heard her speak in this sort of tone. If she'd been addressing me, her tone would have been totally different... My wandering thoughts are interrupted by the rustling bushes, which shake for a moment before several "fluffy balls" of different colors pop out.
170:The multicolored kittens meow, clearly familiar with Chiori Mikami, are hesitant to approach me, the two-legged stranger.
171:Chiori Mikami opens her bag and takes out some prepared cat food and snacks. As soon as one is open, these cautious - but not THAT cautious - little fluffy balls immediately swarm right up to our feet. Just then, a proffered bag of snacks is thrust into my line of sight, so I remove my hands from my ears and take it.
172:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Let's feed them together. They won't be so scared of you then.
173:{character:player}Ahaha! Thanks, Chiori.
174:{character:Chiori Mikami}I-It's not for you! I can't just let them eat while scared.
175:{character:player}Mmhmm, I understand. So what you meant before was coming here to feed these strays? And Riu doesn't know about this?
176:{character:Chiori Mikami}I'm not a child! I don't need Riu to do absolutely everything for me!
178:{character:player}I know, I know. You do pretty well yourself.
179:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Well, naturally.
180:Chiori Mikami turns her head and intently feeds the kitten, only the tip of her red ears revealing her true feelings. She seems happy to have brought a friend to her secret base.
181:However, if Chiori Mikami wasn't originally playing in the children's playground, how did she discover these kittens in such a remote place? I decide to keep this question to myself, in order to maintain the peaceful atmosphere.
182:{character:Chiori Mikami}Eh?!
183:{character:player}Wh-What?
184:Chiori Mikami's exclamation startles me, and I think she's read my mind again.
185:{character:Chiori Mikami}...This isn't right. There's one missing.
186:{character:Chiori Mikami}There were five last time I came. But I haven't seen the little orange one since I got here.
187:{character:player}Your mahjong skills have improved yet again! But I'd expect nothing less from Chiori Mikami, girl genius.
188:As soon as I say this, Chiori Mikami immediately looks at me as she gets off the mahjong table. She walks toward me with an expression of "I know it's you."
189:{character:Chiori Mikami}You don't need to tell me that. But I'm afraid time's running out today, and you'll just have to wait until next time for me to bully you. Let's go, Riu.
190:{character:Riu Kujou}Yes, Miss Chiori.
191:{character:player}...Riu? When did you sneak up on me?
192:Glad I didn't say anything stupid just now. Dodged a bullet.
193:I watch Chiori Mikami and Riu Kujou leave the shrine, then turn to see Ichihime staring at me, lost in thought.
194:Ichihime
195:{character:Ichihime}...A little strange, nyaa.
196:{character:player}What's strange?
197:{character:Ichihime}Just now, Riu quietly approached you like she had something to say, but didn't say it, nyaa.
198:{character:player}Riu?
199:{character:Ichihime}It had to be to ask what tasty food you brought! It smells so good, nyaa!
200:{character:player}...I think that might be what you wanted to ask... Hey hey hey, I'll give it to you later at a restaurant, don't just waltz over here in broad daylight and start sniffing... let alone digging right in!!!
201:...Raising a cat really is a matter of patience! After feeding Ichihime, we play a few rounds of mahjong before the sky darkens and I leave the shrine. In the cool evening air, I keep replaying the day's matches in my mind, and then without even realizing it, I find myself near Chiori Mikami's house.
202:Speaking of which, compared to Ichihime's unorthodox, intuitive style of play, it's a pity that I couldn't see Chiori Mikami's matches just now. She'd probably be more tactical.
203:Bzzz-- The phone rings. Is it actually Riu Kujou?
204:{character:player}Hey, Riu?
205:{character:Riu Kujou}Have you seen Miss Chiori, {var:player_nickname}?
206:{character:player}Didn't she leave with you?
207:{character:Riu Kujou}Yes. We went home after leaving the shrine. I was just preparing a meal when she said she was going to the nearby park for a while, but she still hasn't come back.
208:{character:Riu Kujou}Isn't she with you right now?
209:{character:player}I'm afraid not. However, if it's that little park close to her house... I happen to be in the neighborhood.
210:{character:Riu Kujou}Eh? Really? Great! In that case, could I trouble you to look for her? I'm on my way out the door too!
211:{character:player}Not a problem at all, but... calm down, let me get this straight. When did she say she was heading out?
212:{character:Riu Kujou}At 17:31. She said she'd only be gone for half an hour.
213:{character:player}Is being so frighteningly precise a quality of being a professional maid?... Hang on, it says here that it's exactly 18:00, which technically means it hasn't yet been half an hour.
214:{character:Riu Kujou}She's not in my field of vision, which means there's no way Miss Chiori could get home in the next one minute. And she didn't take her phone with her either. This all makes me worried.
215:{character:player}Very rigorous deduction. However, there are loads of reasons why you may not have heard from her for half an hour. One Han City's a pretty safe place, and this sort of thing isn't like having an accident or going missing, so why don't we wait and see?
216:{character:Riu Kujou}Impossible! What if she did have an accident?!
217:{character:player}...Riu, do you think you might be a little overreacting?
218:{character:Riu Kujou}...
218:{character:Chiori Mikami}...
219:Riu Kujou pauses for a moment. I hear her take a deep breath, and her suddenly raised voice returns to its usual calm.
221:{character:player}What?
222:Then, Riu Kujou tells me something I didn't know before on the phone.
223:{character:Riu Kujou}To be specific, a week ago I had finished preparing dinner and gone to call Miss Chiori down, when something strange happened...
224:Just then, Chiori Mikami's voice comes from outside the bedroom, indicating that her actual location is the small study next door.
225:Riu Kujou clears her head, hurriedly replaces the teddy bear onto the swing, then runs out of the bedroom in response to Chiori Mikami's call.
226:{character:Riu Kujou}That was the first time I learned of their existence. Afterward, whenever I was out with Miss Chiori I felt several times like someone was spying on us from the shadows.
227:{character:player}Does Chiori know about this?
228:{character:Riu Kujou}No, she doesn't. I don't want her to get scared over potentially nothing. Oh, I'm just not good enough, so I've already enrolled in the latest Special Maid Training class to sharpen my anti-surveillance skills!
229:{character:player}You've already done really well, Riu, and I think I have a grasp of the situation. She said she was going to the park, right? Then that's where I'll start looking for her.
230:{character:Riu Kujou}Thank you so much!
231:Given that it's dinner time, there aren't many people in the park. I search the square dancing team, the public mahjong tables, and the children's playground, but find no glimpse of Chiori Mikami anywhere. I have to expand my search to include areas near the park.
232:Since she was only going for half an hour, and didn't take her phone, Chiori Mikami couldn't have gone far. The fact that she's nowhere to be found is a little worrying, but... something's not right.
233:I look around and find the source of the weirdness - I'm clearly the only one nearby, but I feel like I'm being watched.
234:I'm suddenly reminded of the strange event Riu Kujou had told me about... What if it's that mysterious scoundrel? But whoever that is wouldn't have a reason to follow me, surely?
235:I calm the goosebumps across my body, then suddenly rush to where I feel the strange feeling of being watched is coming from.
236:{character:player}Who's there?! Come out!
237:A figure flashes by in a split second, running to a different area. While I didn't get a good look... there's something familiar about that red hairband poking out from the bushes over there.
238:{character:player}...Chiori? Is that you?
239:Whoever it is goes quiet for a couple of seconds, then suddenly reaches out and pulls the hairband down.
240:That's not very subtle!!!
241:I advance a few steps toward where they're hiding, only to hear the bushes rustle and see the person who seems to be Chiori Mikami run farther away.
242:{character:player}...Is Chiori playing some weird version of hide and seek? Why not come out? Riu asked me to find you!
243:???
244:{character:???}... ...
245:{character:???}Meow.
246:The other person doesn't reply directly, but from a distance responds with a surprisingly realistic meow.
247:Why would Chiori Mikami rather use the hackneyed method of imitating a cat to hide herself, instead of just coming out? This is just too strange.
248:The situation is so weird that I can't act rashly. I need to figure out a way to get her to come out first.
249:I decide to use some mind games to trap this odd stalker, so I yell--
250:{character:player}Chiori Mikami's skill at mahjong is just average!
251:{character:Chiori Mikami}You peasant! Let's have a match right now if you think you're up for it!
252:The girl who suddenly springs up from behind the bushes has her hands on her hips, a completely unbelieving expression on her face. Good, it's her.
253:{character:player}Haha, finally willing to come out, eh?
254:My tone is too proud, and Chiori Mikami's eyes flash with pure fury.
255:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Argh! You despicable, cunning, shameless, creep!!!
256:{character:player}You're the one who followed me, hid when discovered, then pretended to be a cat when found out, no?
257:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Nonsense. Clearly it's you, a strange commoner, who suddenly appeared in the place I was passing through, harboring unknown intentions! Your sneaky maliciousness seemed like you wanted to shove me in a sack, so of course I wasn't going to come out!
258:{character:player}You're just making things up!
259:{character:Chiori Mikami}You've got sinister motives!
260:{character:player}Come clean!
261:{character:Chiori Mikami}My business is none of yours!
262:{character:player}See?! You still say you're not hiding anything from me! Let something slip?
263:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Just wait until I go back and tell Riu about what you've said and your total arrogance.
264:{character:player}I apologize, my lady.
265:I raise my hand in surrender to declare a "truce". The wise adapt to the situation, and while mind games are useful, it's also wise to know when to stop. There's no point in doing things that will only hurt yourself.
266:And anyway, now that Chiori Mikami's been found, it's better to let Riu Kujou know so she doesn't worry.
267:I send a message to Riu Kujou.
268:{character:Riu Kujou}(Text message) Found her? That's great! Where are you?
271:{character:player}Alright... We're...
272:I stop as I'm just about to type and look around. There are no evident landmarks nearby. Recalling that Chiori Mikami lives in the area, I look at her.
273:{character:player}Chiori? Chiori? Chioriiii?!
274:{character:Chiori Mikami}I'm not talking to you if you're just gonna repeat yourself!
275:{character:player}Uh, I mean, what is this place? Riu wants to confirm where you are.
276:{character:Chiori Mikami}...This place... this... is a street near my house.
277:{character:player}Huh? That description won't be of much help. Could you be a bit more specific?
278:{character:Chiori Mikami}...A pretty narrow street near my house!
279:{character:player}Come on, don't be like that. That's not what I meant by specific. Can't you tell me something like what direction it is from your house, or the street's name... Wait...
280:I catch her flash of embarrassment, and it suddenly hits me.
281:{character:player}So... Chiori, were you secretly following me because you're lost?
282:{character:Chiori Mikami}Vicious slander! I, Chiori Mikami, could never get lost!!!!
283:Despite Chiori Mikami's ear-splitting denial, her sudden blushing betrays her.
284:Unwilling to admit to being lost so close to home, preferring to "follow the familiar face" than ask for help... Since these are the facts, all I can say is--
285:{character:player}Well, that's classic Chiori.
285:Well, that's classic Chiori.
286:{character:Chiori Mikami}...{var:player_nickname}...
287:{character:player}Now, now, don't do anything rash... All I meant was that your ability to think on your feet and get out of trouble is amazing!
288:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Hmph. Don't think I don't know when I'm being insulted. But Chiori doesn't waste time on idiots. Hand it over!
289:{character:player}Good thing I'm so smart.
290:{character:Chiori Mikami}You? Smart? That's a joke. Now give it to me!
291:Chiori Mikami stalks toward me, seething. I'm ready to defend myself against a vicious attack, but she suddenly reaches out and grabs my phone. She snaps several photos and sends them to Riu Kujou.
292:{character:Chiori Mikami}Morons will be morons. Isn't this a more effective way of letting her know where we are?
295:{character:player}...Fine.
296:Chiori Mikami tosses my phone back to me in a huff. Now that I'm closer to her, I suddenly realize something about her is different from normal - her hair is a little messy, and there's visible dust on her normally-pristine skirt and sleeves. There's no way her hiding place would have made her that dusty.
297:{character:Chiori Mikami}What are you looking at?! Turn around!
298:Sensing my gaze, Chiori Mikami puts her hands behind her back in frustration. Apparently, being not beautiful enough is one of the reasons why she's unwilling to come out and meet me. But what actually happened to her? Could it be connected with that "scoundrel"?
299:{character:player}Can you tell me where you just were, Chiori? How come you were lost?
300:{character:Chiori Mikami}Shut it! There's no way I'm gonna tell you. You'd just laugh at me!
301:{character:player}I'm not asking so I can make fun of you, Chiori, but because I'm worried. Your safety is my priority, so I'll force you out of hiding and make sure you're really okay, even if it makes you angry.
302:{character:Chiori Mikami}...You've got a really smart mouth on you.
303:Perhaps it's my serious tone, but Chiori Mikami only pouts as the rage in her eyes gradually subsides.
304:{character:player}Please, won't you tell me?
305:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Hmph, look at your pitiful face. I suppose that if I don't tell you, you'll probably not be able to stay focused and keep losing at mahjong. And if you, a fragile commoner, become so desperate over losing that you give up on life, it will only cause me more trouble.
306:{character:player}You're completely right. So, you'll tell me?
307:{character:Chiori Mikami}...I went to rescue a kitten.
308:{character:player}A kitten?
309:{character:Chiori Mikami}There's a calico stray cat in the park. She's pretty vicious and won't let me pet her, but she did give birth to a litter of kittens. They're totally exposed to the elements, so I come to feed them when I can. I was about to head back after feeding them today as usual, when I noticed that one of the kittens was missing. The mother led me to where her kitten was trapped, and I went to rescue it.
310:{character:Chiori Mikami}And that's it. That's all that happened.
311:{character:player}Huh?
312:{character:Chiori Mikami}You'd better not say you didn't hear, and want me to repeat myself.
313:{character:player}No, no, I heard!
314:{character:player}Ahaha! So that's what happened. Look at you and your kind heart, Chiori. Does Riu know about this?
315:{character:Chiori Mikami}I'm not a child! I don't need Riu to do absolutely everything for me!
316:So that's how it is. From how much Riu Kujou looks after Chiori Mikami, if she knew about this trivial matter she'd probably immediately add "take care of lady's park kitties" to her daily list of tasks.
317:{character:player}Okay, I understand. You do pretty well yourself. So, where's this kitten you saved?
318:{character:Chiori Mikami}Its mother carried it off as soon as it was rescued.
319:{character:player}Wow... so thankless.
320:{character:Chiori Mikami}That's just how cats are. They won't be picked on if they're vigilant. After all, not everyone is as kind and lovely as me!
321:{character:player}Hmm, I suppose you're right. Well, at least Riu and I can rest easy now...
322:Having heard this much, and not just about Chiori Mikami getting lost, I have my own suspicions about Riu Kujou's "scoundrel". I'll have a chat with her when I head back later.
323:{character:Chiori Mikami}I've already told you what you wanted to know, so stop making me stand here! Show me the way out! Index and I want to have a bath!
324:Chiori Mikami commands me imperiously, while clutching her smudged plushie handbag.
325:{character:player}Immediately! As you wish!
326:We make it safely back to Chiori Mikami's house, and while she's in the bath I fill in Riu Kujou on what happened.
327:{character:Riu Kujou}Phew... Can't believe that sort of thing happened... But anyway, thank you so much for your help.
328:{character:player}Don't mention it. Anyone would do the same.
329:{character:Riu Kujou}Oh yeah, speaking of the scoundrel... They left another clue. Come with me.
330:{character:player}Okay. I've got my own ideas about their true identity anyway, so this might help verify.
331:Riu Kujou and I go to the front door, where she takes out a cardboard box and opens it for me to take a look. Inside is a pretty large, dead mouse.
332:{character:Riu Kujou}This time they left this right outside the glass door to Miss Chiori's balcony. I was worried that she might see it, so scooped it up and put it in the box. Really, so repulsive!
333:{character:player}Oh... Could you show me the balcony, Riu? There might be something to confirm the culprit's identity.
334:Riu Kujou hesitates briefly, then nods.
335:{character:player}Aha! Seems I was right. Take a look here.
336:I search carefully after following Riu Kujou to Chiori Mikami's balcony, and find the "evidence" on the girlishly-decorated swing - stuck in its chains is a pinch of multicolored... cat hair.
337:{character:Riu Kujou}...Cat hair?
338:{character:player}That's right. Felines have a habit of presenting their prey to benefactors. I suspect that the only one who can stealthily climb up to such a high balcony, spy without being discovered every day, and also leave such a "horrible" gift is... one of the cats that Chiori's insisted on feeding, the mother of that litter of kittens.
339:{character:Riu Kujou}I see.
340:{character:player}Right. One person's trash is another's treasure, but this seemingly ferocious cat's way of saying thanks really is a little hard for humans to accept. I feel kinda sorry for you, Riu, as I think you could find quite a few gifts like this for Chiori in the near future.
341:{character:Riu Kujou}Got it. I'll take care of it. But instead of feeling sorry for me, I suggest you figure out your next steps.
342:{character:player}What do you mean?
343:{character:Riu Kujou}Miss Chiori just informed me that today you seemed to know things that you weren't supposed to. She was very firm that I must deal with you tonight.
344:{character:player}...Objection! Didn't I bring her back after she'd gotten lost? Don't you think this way of repaying a favor is a little unreasonable?
345:{character:Riu Kujou}That's a different matter. Miss Chiori has decided to let you stay for dinner as a token of gratitude. In the meantime, think carefully about how to beg forgiveness.
346:Fine. It is what it is. Looks like I'm going to have to value the time I spend with the young lady, strive to make a good impression, and earn some leniency.
347:{character:player}I want to pick up a few pointers from you, as I think your mahjong skills go from strength to strength. I don't know if you'd give me the opportunity?
348:Mahjong is the mutual interest that we're most familiar with, and surely it won't be any problem using this as a way in. Sure enough, Chiori Mikami's expression immediately turns smug as soon as the words have left my mouth.
349:{character:Chiori Mikami}Hmph. So that's your plan. You know you're not the only one who wants to exchange mahjong tips with me. Whether or not you earn this privilege depends on your performance. Let's play!
350:{character:player}Bring it on!
351:To prove my worth, I enlist Ichihime and Riu Kujou, and together with Chiori Mikami we play an East Wind round. I have only mediocre luck today, however, and in the end I come second to Chiori Mikami.
352:{character:Chiori Mikami}Pff. Average skill at best, and no sign of progress since last time. I have no interest in comparing notes now. Let's call it a day, and I hope you don't lose too badly next time.
353:{character:player}Huh? Hang on, you aren't going to play anymore, Chiori?
354:{character:Chiori Mikami}I have other things to do today. Let's go, Riu.
355:{character:Riu Kujou}Coming!
492:{character:Riu Kujou}...Seems I was mistaken. You're not that important to my lady, at least not in mahjong, as she doesn't view your skill too favorably. In this case, just forget everything you heard today.
357:Riu Kujou follows Chiori Mikami, and they both leave.
358:It appears that if I want to get close to Chiori Mikami, I need to get better at mahjong until I can beat her. As it is, my protection mission is over before it even started.
359:I decide to sweet talk this young lady into showing herself. So I do my best and, in the gentlest tone possible, speak toward the place she's hiding...
360:{character:player}I bet that the world's most beautiful, adorable, totally perfect genius is hiding over there - Miss Chiori Mikami!
361:Chiori Mikami doesn't take the bait, and actually moves farther away.
362:I try my very best, but to no avail. Bewildered, all I can do is head back. Luckily I discover that, although she won't come out, as long as I keep moving, she'll keep following me in secret.
363:As soon as I've worked this out, I simply inform Riu Kujou and then head straight for Chiori Mikami's house. By the time I arrive, Riu Kujou is already waiting at the door.
364:I shoot Riu Kujou a look, then hear a "whoosh" noise as a figure darts past so fast I can't get a good look at them.
365:The door slams shut with a bang.
366:{character:player}Chiori?
367:{character:Chiori Mikami}No Chiori here! You're mistaken!
368:...She must be fine, moving that quickly, with that firm voice, right? I exchange a look with Riu Kujou.
369:However, it's clear that Chiori Mikami has decided not to see me today and, with Riu Kujou's persuasion, I leave in confusion.
370:The next day, I once again see the unbeatable Chiori Mikami at the Mahjong Soul Shrine, accompanied by Riu Kujou. I think back on yesterday's unfinished business, and quietly approach Riu to ask how things went after I left.
371:{character:Riu Kujou}Oh, you're still thinking of that? That's good of you.
372:{character:Riu Kujou}The matter's closed, but you still need to keep the existence of the scoundrel a secret from Miss Chiori, understand?
373:{character:player}Mmhmm, got it. Don't worry, I'll keep my mouth shut.
374:{character:Riu Kujou}Good.
375:I didn't expect Riu Kujou to get to the bottom of it all in just one day. Under the strictest confidence of the maid, this tale of Chiori Mikami will remain a secret to me forever.
376:So cocky... It wouldn't be surprising if she gets bundled into a sack one day.
377:Her mahjong skills have improved yet again! But that's normal for Chiori, girl genius.
378:Just as Riu Kujou says she wants to talk with me, a dire voice emanates from a nearby table, echoing in the Mahjong Soul Shrine and frightening all who hear it.
379:One Week Earlier, Chiori Mikami's House
380:So Riu Kujou takes me to see Chiori Mikami, and I request to go with them...
381:I really like you, Chiori, so I would love to get to know you a bit more.
382:I think Chiori's mahjong skills are amazing, and I want to compare notes.
383:{character:player}I really like you, Chiori, and would love to get to know you a bit more. I don't know if you'd be willing to give me the chance?
384:At this, Chiori Mikami's face blushes visibly.
385:{character:Chiori Mikami}...L-Like what exactly? I've heard this excuse so many times now, it's really getting old!
386:{character:Chiori Mikami}However...Since your thick skull probably can't actually think of a better excuse so, considering your honesty, I suppose I can let you follow me. But only from a distance!
387:{character:Chiori Mikami}Let's go, hmph.
388:{character:player}Sure, not a problem!
389:Chiori Mikami may have sounded reluctant, but she can't help hopping a little and humming a tune as she walks away.
390:Indeed, being frank and direct is the most effective approach. Riu Kujou quietly gives me a thumbs up as she passes, then immediately makes a fist and brandishes it at me. I nod silently to show I understand.
391:Seeing Chiori Mikami's lively figure also lightens my mood, and I immediately match their pace.
392:After spending the whole afternoon playing mahjong, the evening is already upon us. So we head directly to Chiori Mikami's house when leave the shrine.
393:The journey back is uneventful, with no sign of the mysterious scoundrel Riu Kujou has mentioned. But when we reach a park near her house, Chiori Mikami suddenly stops.
394:{character:Chiori Mikami}I want to go for a walk in the park. You go back and get dinner going, Riu. I'm sure it'll take a lot of time to plan for someone with an unpredictable appetite.
395:{character:Riu Kujou}I... Miss, why don't you just come back too? Going to the park at this hour might be a little dangerous.
396:{character:Chiori Mikami}Eh? What're you talking about, Riu? What's dangerous about the park?
397:{character:Riu Kujou}I-I mean...
398:{character:player}Well, since I'm here anyway, I might as well go with Chiori.
399:I interrupt their conversation while simultaneously sending a sneaky text message. Riu Kujou feels her phone vibrate, takes it out, and glances at the screen, while I smile like nothing's happened.
400:{character:player}If you don't get going, Riu, there won't be enough time to make dinner.
401:{character:Riu Kujou}...You're right. I'm not bothered about you, but I can't let Miss Chiori go hungry.
402:{character:Riu Kujou}I'll go back then. Dinner won't take too long, so don't be too late, Miss.
403:{character:Chiori Mikami}I know, I know. You just love to worry, Riu.
404:I'd just told Riu in the message that I'd stay with Chiori Mikami all the time, and would take her home at the first sign of any danger.
405:Perhaps considering the proximity to Chiori Mikami's house, Riu Kujou finally relented.
406:"You're solely responsible if anything happens to her!" Of course, she didn't forget to warn me with another serious message.
407:{character:player}Alright, let's go to the park! ...Why are you looking at me like that?
408:{character:Chiori Mikami}Well, idiocy's infectious, and even Riu's not immune. You both have "guilty" plastered over your faces, I'm not even interested to see what else you've got up your sleeves. Now, tell me, what were you secretly communicating?
409:...She actually knows?!
410:{character:player}Well, you overthink things, Chiori. I was just... Begging Riu to give us a chance to be alone together!
411:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Really?
412:{character:player}Yes!
413:{character:Chiori Mikami}...Tsk, is that all? Well, let's go have some fun then.
414:{character:player}Great!
415:Cicadas sing slowly as night falls in the city park, and birds descend from the clouds to settle in shady trees. There aren't many people under the trees, though playing children occasionally pass us, and we hear the voices of their parents calling them home coming from afar.
416:Chiori Mikami leads me toward the children's playground, not a soul in sight among its brightly colored furnishings. Speaking of which, Chiori herself isn't that much older than those children... Could she have been waiting for everyone else to leave before she came here?
417:{character:Chiori Mikami}Stop.
418:{character:player}???
419:{character:Chiori Mikami}Childish thinking. I don't like playing with these anymore.
420:{character:player}...You can tell?
421:{character:Chiori Mikami}Ha, you don't even try to deny it. You really were thinking it!
422:{character:player}...Fell for it.
423:{character:Chiori Mikami}Hmph. Come here.
424:Chiori Mikami waves at me, beckoning me to keep up. Curious, I follow her example, walking slowly across the playground, through some bushes, and along some winding paths to a hidden corner of the park.
425:{character:Chiori Mikami}Ahem... you, cover your ears.
426:What on earth does she want to do? Should I listen to her?
427:
429:Cover ears.
430:Pretend to cover ears.
431:Could you have got the number wrong?
433:Why don't we split up?
434:At dusk
435:In the park
436:
437:
438:{character:???}Meow--
439:Then, in the distance, there's another meow. Chiori Mikami and I look at the same time to find a large, full-grown calico cat. It approaches, rubs our legs, meows twice, and runs off a few steps. It looks back and, seeing that we haven't moved, meows anxiously.
440:{character:Chiori Mikami}This is the mother cat. She's never let me get close before, let alone voluntarily come to say hi.
441:{character:player}Something must have happened. Let's follow her.
442:We follow the cat all over the place, until she eventually stops near a remote, dried-up canal. She starts meowing, and a feeble cry responds weakly.
443:Chiori Mikami and I squat down to look and sure enough, there's the lost orange kitten. We don't know what it had been through, but right now it's stuck behind a fence at the far end of the canal, unable to move. Seeing us coming, its cries get even more plaintive.
444:{character: Chiori Mikami}Don't be scared! We're here to rescue you. {var:player_nickname}, help me look after Index.
445:Before I can reply, Chiori Mikami thrusts her plushie handbag at me, rolls up her sleeves, and slips into the canal.
446:The disused canal isn't deep and, while it might be dry, it's also full of cobwebs and dust. Chiori Mikami frowns, but doesn't hesitate in reaching behind the fence and clearing the stones that have the kitten trapped. Too late to help, I can only watch Chiori Mikami nervously, ready to ensure her safety.
448:{character:Chiori Mikami}It's okay. You can come out now.
450:{character:Chiori Mikami}Remember to look after your kids next time!
451:However, the scene in my imagination of cats understanding human speech and thanking the two-legged beasts does not materialize. Instead, the calico cat looks at us warily, then quick as a flash picks up the little orange kitten and disappears into the shadows.
452:{character:player}...Well, it's in cats' nature to be wary of humans.
453:Having thought that, I look at Chiori Mikami. She's not upset with the cat's "callousness" in the slightest, but jumps up, turns around, and walks back.
454:{character:Chiori Mikami}Hmph, let's go. You may be useless, but at least you've got a positive attitude. Come to my place for dinner.
455:Thanks to the rescue operation just now, her sleeves and skirt are covered in dust. It's the first time I've seen her looking so disheveled.
457:{character:player}...What?
458:{character:Chiori Mikami}You go first.
459:{character:player}Huh?
460:{character:Chiori Mikami}Quickly!
461:I don't know why, but I do as I'm told. I'd followed the cat all the way here, so the surrounding paths are all unfamiliar. I should be able to remember the way back, as long as we... go... slowly.
462:Suddenly, a thought strikes me.
463:{character:player}So, Chiori, you couldn't...
464:{character:Chiori Mikami}Impossible! There's no way I don't know the way back!
465:{character:player}Ha! You didn't need to be asked either! We're even now.
466:{character:Chiori Mikami}...OOOHHHHH! You despicable, cunning, shameless, creep!!!
467:My happy mood automatically translates this into words of praise. Turns out the mahjong girl genius is a little bad at directions, and that's an unexpected bonus this trip.
468:{character:Chiori Mikami}Fool, do you think I have as bad a memory as you?! Maybe we should split up.
469:{character:Chiori Mikami}Well, looks like there's nothing for it.
470:Chiori Mikami's house
471:Chiori Mikami's balcony
472:
473:Coax her out with kind words.
474:Use mind games to get her to come out.
475:{character:player}(Text message) It's just nearby.
477:{character:Riu Kujou}(Text message) Tell me the location. I need to confirm your safety.
479:Well, it's me after all. 
480:{character:Riu Kujou}(Text message) Received.
481:The next day
482:{character:player}Huh? The scoundrel? Is that still a thing??
483:{character:Riu Kujou}It is, after all, the meaning of my existence as a maid to clean up all filth from my lady's sight. This is only proper.
484:Looking at Riu Kujou's posture, which suggests she is always ready to launch an attack due to her year-round practice of taekwondo, it's not difficult to imagine how she might have "cleaned up" those scoundrels.
485:So that's how it is. From how much Riu Kujou looks after Chiori Mikami, if she knew about this trivial matter she'd probably immediately add "take care of lady's park kitties" to her daily list of tasks.
493:The calico cat leads the way and clearly understands that we're rescuing her kitten. While she paces nervously around me, she doesn't interfere until Chiori Mikami successfully saves the kitten.
487:I carefully take the kitten from Chiori Mikami's hand, then hold out my own to help her out of the canal, before gently depositing the kitten in front of its mother.
489:Suddenly Chiori Mikami, who is walking in front, comes to a complete stop. She pauses, turns her head, and then walks quickly behind me... I think I see a flash of confusion in her eyes, but it's gone in an instant - if it was ever there.
490:{character:Riu Kujou}Oh, I'm sorry. I'm a little nervous as it's not safe around Miss Chiori these days.
